{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit navigation engine.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Types","title":"Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/UrlOpener"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Navigation-Article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/navigation-article"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Actions-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AI-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/App-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Callouts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Clipboard-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Emojis-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/External-Keyboards-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Feedback-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Fonts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Layout-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Localization-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom keyboard extension may have to open URLs or trigger deep links, for instance to open the app or System Settings. But since a keyboard extension can’t use ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UIApplication.shared"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", opening URLs can be difficult.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit provides keyboard extensions with ways to open URLs without "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"UIApplication.shared","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". Use this to open any URL with ease.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Opening a URL from a Keyboard Extension","type":"heading","anchor":"Opening-a-URL-from-a-Keyboard-Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The best way to open a URL from a keyboard extension, is to use a native SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Link","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can also trigger a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/url(_:id:)","isActive":true},{"text":" action to let the main ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/actionHandler","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" open it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS 26 and later requires Full Access to open URLs with both native links and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardActionHandler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". You should ask the user to enable Full Access if you need to open URLs from your keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"level":2,"text":"Opening System Settings","type":"heading","anchor":"Opening-System-Settings"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit defines a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/URL\/systemSettings"},{"type":"text","text":" URL that can be used to open your app in System Settings. This can be used to help users enable the keyboard, enable Full Access, etc."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your keyboard navigates to the System Settings root instead of your app, try adding an empty settings bundle to your app target."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Opening the Main App from a Keyboard Extension","anchor":"Opening-the-Main-App-from-a-Keyboard-Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The best way to open the main app from its keyboard extension, is to trigger the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/openMainApp(_:withReason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" action to let the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/actionHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" open the app. You can provide an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to tell the app why it was opened.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the main app, you can then use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReason","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReasonCase","isActive":true},{"text":" to see why it was opened, and show contextual information if needed. The open reason will automatically reset when the main app is sent to the background.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit will automatically open your main app with the open reason ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" when starting dictation, then try to navigate back to the keyboard once dictation has been started.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"tip"},{"anchor":"Returning-to-the-Keyboard-Extension-from-the-Main-App","text":"Returning to the Keyboard Extension from the Main App","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" has a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext\/hostApplicationBundleId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (see the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" article for more information) that can be mapped to a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", you can trigger the app’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication\/open(withAction:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to return to the keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"However, since KeyboardKit only knows about the most common apps, you can’t rely on this. You should therefore instruct your users on how to tap the top leading back button to return to the keyboard, when no host application can be resolved available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Navigation","role":"article","images":[{"identifier":"Feature-Navigation.jpg","type":"